# ---- 752 Introduction to Fire Science ----
H("752.d.4",3,"A fire service recruit reviews radio traffic, written reports, hand signals and face-to-face briefings. These show the:","different types of communication used in the fire service",["parts of a hose","classes of fire","kinds of ladders"],"Fire crews use verbal, written, radio and nonverbal communication.")
H("752.d.4",4,"A firefighter uses a hand signal to tell a pump operator to stop water when a roaring engine drowns out voices. This is:","nonverbal communication",["written communication","a report","a letter"],"Signals work when noise blocks speech.")
H("752.d.1.A",3,"A recruit sets the goal 'Pass the physical agility test in 12 weeks by training four days a week.' This is built using the steps for a:","SMART goal",["random wish","vague plan","daydream"],"SMART goals are specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound.")
H("752.d.1.A",4,"In a SMART goal, the 'M' stands for:","measurable",["magical","mandatory","moderate"],"A measurable goal can be tracked.")
H("752.d.1.B",3,"A student explains that tracking daily sit-ups, finishing a 5K and improving personal bests each show different benefits of setting goals. These are:","process, outcome and performance benefits of SMART goals",["no benefits","only prizes","only penalties"],"SMART goals help focus effort and track progress.")
H("752.d.1.B",4,"Writing a goal with a deadline mainly helps a recruit to:","stay focused and measure progress",["avoid planning","delay effort","remove choices"],"Deadlines give structure.")
H("752.d.1.C",3,"After setting a goal to earn a fire certification, a recruit lists tasks, resources, due dates and possible obstacles. This is creating an:","action plan",["excuse list","wish list","grocery list"],"Action plans break goals into steps.")
H("752.d.1.C",4,"A good action plan for a SMART goal includes:","clear tasks, deadlines and resources",["only a slogan","only a dream","no dates"],"Actions need tasks and timelines.")
H("752.d.2.A",3,"A student compares job duties and hiring needs for private-sector fire protection jobs such as industrial brigades. This identifies:","employment requirements and roles in private fire protection",["public sector only","school jobs","farm jobs"],"Private employers hire fire protection staff.")
H("752.d.2.A",4,"A refinery's fire brigade is an example of:","private-sector fire protection",["a volunteer city department","a federal agency","a state park"],"Industry runs its own brigades.")
H("752.d.2.B",3,"A recruit studies how municipal fire departments hire firefighters and what they do on shift. This identifies roles in:","city-run career fire services",["only airports","only forests","only ships"],"Municipal departments serve cities.")
H("752.d.2.B",4,"A career municipal firefighter is typically employed by a:","city or town",["private yacht club","movie studio","bank"],"Municipal means city-run.")
H("752.d.2.C",3,"A student explores jobs in a county fire marshal's office and a rural volunteer department. This identifies:","roles in county, rural and volunteer fire services",["school roles","mining roles","retail roles"],"Many fire jobs are county and volunteer.")
H("752.d.2.C",4,"Volunteer firefighters serve primarily by:","responding to calls with training but often without regular pay",["working full time salaried","only teaching","only cooking"],"Volunteers serve their community.")
H("752.d.2.D",3,"A recruit researches Texas A&M Forest Service wildland roles and airport firefighting careers. This identifies:","roles in wildland and airport fire protection",["restaurant jobs","office jobs only","bank jobs"],"Specialty fire jobs exist.")
H("752.d.2.D",4,"An aircraft rescue and firefighting crew is stationed at:","an airport",["a library","a school cafeteria","a mall"],"ARFF protects aircraft operations.")
H("752.d.2.E",3,"A city posts a firefighter opening that requires an application, written exam, physical ability test and interview. These are:","common employment processes for public sector firefighters",["random steps","hiring rumors","no steps"],"Hiring is a multi-step process.")
H("752.d.2.E",4,"After passing a written test, a firefighter candidate commonly completes:","a physical ability test and interview",["a cooking class","a map contest","a sports bet"],"Selection includes physical testing.")
H("752.d.3.A",3,"In Texas, a recruit completes required courses and passes exams to become a certified firefighter under the state commission. This describes:","the firefighter certification process in Texas",["a school diploma","a driver license","a library card"],"Certification is state-regulated.")
H("752.d.3.A",4,"The Texas agency that certifies firefighters is the:","Texas Commission on Fire Protection",["Texas Lottery Commission","Texas Racing Commission","Texas Parks Department"],"TCFP certifies fire personnel.")
H("752.d.3.B",3,"A student sorts a college degree, a basic firefighter academy course and a state license into groups. This differentiates:","education, training and certification requirements",["recipes","sports roles","art styles"],"Each requirement serves a different purpose.")
H("752.d.3.B",4,"Which is an example of certification rather than education?","a state-issued firefighter certificate",["a high school diploma","a science textbook","a lecture note"],"A certificate verifies standards are met.")
H("752.d.3.C",3,"A recruit reads how the state sets minimum standards, approves training programs and reviews records. This explains the:","role of the TCFP in firefighter certification",["role of schools","role of banks","role of insurers"],"TCFP sets and enforces standards.")
H("752.d.3.C",4,"The TCFP helps protect the public by:","setting minimum standards for fire personnel",["selling equipment","writing menus","building stations"],"Standards ensure competence.")
H("752.d.5.A",3,"A firefighter adjusts how she speaks to a frightened child and then to a fellow officer, while listening and watching body cues. This shows:","key elements of adaptive communication",["one-size-fits-all speech","avoiding people","silence"],"Adaptive communication fits the audience.")
H("752.d.5.A",4,"During a fire station briefing, which action shows active listening by a recruit?","paying full attention and restating what the officer said",["interrupting the officer","checking a phone","changing the subject"],"Confirming prevents errors.")
H("752.d.5.B",3,"On a crew, clear, flexible communication helps members avoid mistakes at emergencies. This shows the:","importance of adaptive communication in the fire service",["uselessness of talking","value of silence","need for secrecy"],"Good communication improves safety and teamwork.")
H("752.d.5.B",4,"Adaptive communication improves fire service operations by:","reducing misunderstandings among crew and the public",["raising confusion","slowing action","hiding facts"],"Clarity prevents mistakes.")
H("752.d.5.C",3,"Members of a truck company share tasks, back each other up and speak respectfully. These are:","interpersonal skills that support effective teamwork",["selfish habits","solo skills","rumors"],"Teamwork needs interpersonal skill.")
H("752.d.5.C",4,"Which trait best supports teamwork on a fire crew?","reliability and respect for others",["secrecy","competition for credit","arrogance"],"Reliable, respectful members build trust.")
H("752.d.5.D",3,"Two firefighters disagree on a chore schedule, and they compromise by alternating duties. This is a conflict resolution strategy called:","compromising",["avoiding","competing","ignoring"],"Compromise meets in the middle.")
H("752.d.5.D",4,"Which conflict strategy involves giving in to the other person's wishes?","accommodating",["competing","avoiding","collaborating"],"Accommodating yields to the other side.")
H("752.d.6.A",3,"A recruit learns that old social media posts, peer pressure, drug use and a criminal record can block a fire career. This discusses:","personal choices that impact a fire service career",["no impacts","only school","only sports"],"Conduct affects hiring.")
H("752.d.6.A",4,"Why do fire departments review a candidate's social media?","Posts can show judgment and character",["to find pictures","to give awards","to sell ads"],"Conduct online reflects professionalism.")
H("752.d.6.B",3,"A student matches the Texas A&M Forest Service, the State Fire Marshal's Office, the TCFP and Texas A&M Engineering Extension Service to their roles. This analyzes:","the four Texas State Fire Service agencies",["four sports teams","four banks","four schools"],"Four agencies support fire service.")
H("752.d.6.B",4,"The agency that provides firefighter training courses across Texas is:","Texas A&M Engineering Extension Service (TEEX)",["Texas Lottery Commission","Texas Racing Commission","Texas Education Agency"],"TEEX trains first responders.")
H("752.d.6.C",3,"A class compares the firefighter's code of ethics from national fire organizations. This identifies and compares:","professional codes of ethics relevant to the fire service",["menus","dress codes only","sports rules"],"Ethics guide conduct.")
H("752.d.6.C",4,"A code of ethics for firefighters generally stresses:","honesty, integrity and service to the public",["profit","fame","secrecy"],"Core values guide the service.")
H("752.d.6.D",3,"On duty, a firefighter in Texas is required to respond to a person in danger because of a legal obligation to help. This is the:","legal concept of Duty to Act",["right to ignore","duty to hide","duty to leave"],"Duty to Act binds public safety responders.")
H("752.d.6.D",4,"Because of the Duty to Act, a firefighter who ignores a call that is within their duties may face:","legal and professional consequences",["a bonus","a trophy","a vacation"],"Failure to act can lead to liability.")
H("752.d.6.E",3,"A bystander gives first aid at a crash scene and is protected from most lawsuits by the Texas Good Samaritan Act. This describes:","legal protection for people who give emergency aid in good faith",["a penalty","a tax","a licence"],"The Act protects good-faith helpers.")
H("752.d.6.E",4,"The Texas Good Samaritan Act is found in the:","Texas Civil Practice and Remedies Code",["Texas Penal Code only","Texas Tax Code","Texas Education Code"],"Chapter 74 covers Good Samaritan.")
H("752.d.7.A",3,"A timeline shows the Great Chicago Fire, steam pumpers, motorized apparatus and thermal imaging cameras. These are:","key milestones and technological advances in the fire service",["recipes","sports trophies","fashion trends"],"Technology changed fire fighting.")
H("752.d.7.A",4,"A major change in the fire service over time was the shift from horse-drawn wagons to:","motorized apparatus",["canoes","bicycles","sailboats"],"Motorization sped response.")
H("752.d.7.B",3,"A class sorts a city ordinance, a state fire code and a national model code. This differentiates:","local, state and federal fire laws and model codes and standards",["school rules","parking laws only","movie rules"],"Fire law has several layers.")
H("752.d.7.B",4,"NFPA codes are often adopted by governments as:","model codes and standards",["school rules","tax forms","hunting rules"],"Models are adopted into law.")
H("752.d.7.C",3,"After a deadly theater fire, cities required more exits and sprinklers in public buildings. This explains how:","fire losses influenced building and fire codes",["fires were ignored","codes were removed","exits were closed"],"Tragedies drive code change.")
H("752.d.7.C",4,"Many fire code requirements for exits and alarms came from:","lessons learned from past deadly fires",["fashion","ads","sports"],"Codes evolve from losses.")
H("752.d.8.A",3,"A student describes a pumper, ladder truck and rescue truck as structural firefighting rigs. This identifies:","structural firefighting apparatus",["boats","tractors","carts"],"Apparatus serve different tasks.")
H("752.d.8.A",4,"A ladder truck is mainly designed to give firefighters:","aerial access to upper floors and roofs",["extra beds","cooking space","a fuel tank"],"Aerial ladders reach height.")
H("752.d.8.B",3,"A brush truck and a water tender are used to fight grass and forest fires. These are:","wildland firefighting apparatus",["ships","buses","cranes"],"Wildland rigs serve off-road fires.")
H("752.d.8.B",4,"A water tender at a rural wildfire is used to:","carry large amounts of water to the fire",["haul firewood","tow houses","lay roads"],"Tenders move water.")
H("752.d.8.C",3,"At an airport, a large rig can spray foam on a burning aircraft quickly. This is an:","aircraft rescue firefighting apparatus",["ambulance","street sweeper","school bus"],"ARFF trucks carry foam.")
H("752.d.8.C",4,"Aircraft rescue firefighting vehicles carry large amounts of:","foam and extinguishing agent",["groceries","fuel for planes only","tickets"],"Foam smothers fuel fires.")
H("752.d.8.D",3,"A firefighter fights a house fire in a helmet, coat, boots and breathing apparatus, but a wildland firefighter wears lighter gear. This identifies:","structural, wildland and aircraft firefighting PPE",["costumes","school uniforms","sports gear"],"PPE fits the hazard.")
H("752.d.8.D",4,"Compared with structural gear, wildland PPE is generally:","lighter and made for heat and long wear",["heavier","made of plastic","the same"],"Wildland work demands mobility.")
H("752.d.8.E",3,"A gated wye, a hose clamp and a manifold are examples of:","appliances used by structural firefighters",["cooking tools","garden tools","carpentry tools"],"Appliances manage water flow.")
H("752.d.8.E",4,"A hose clamp is used to:","stop water flow in a hose line",["cut hose","roll hose","heat hose"],"Clamps pinch hose closed.")
H("752.d.8.F",3,"A halligan bar, axe and pike pole are carried on engines for forcing doors and pulling ceilings. These are:","tools used by structural firefighters",["kitchen tools","office tools","art tools"],"Hand tools support entry and overhaul.")
H("752.d.8.F",4,"A halligan tool is used primarily to:","force open doors and windows",["measure water","carry hose","write reports"],"Halligans pry.")
H("752.d.8.G",3,"A pulaski, a drip torch and a fire rake are carried on wildfire lines. These are:","tools used by wildland firefighters",["kitchen tools","office tools","tile tools"],"Wildland tools clear fuel.")
H("752.d.8.G",4,"A pulaski combines an axe with a:","grubbing hoe (adze)",["wrench","hammer only","saw"],"The pulaski digs and chops.")
H("752.d.8.H",3,"A crew uses large-diameter supply hose and smaller lightweight forestry hose for a brush fire. This differentiates:","hoses used by structural and wildland firefighters",["ropes","cables","pipes"],"Hose types suit the fire.")
H("752.d.8.H",4,"Lightweight wildland hose is useful because crews often:","carry it long distances over rough ground",["never move","drive on it","bury it"],"Weight matters on the fireline.")
H("752.d.9.A",3,"A fire chief explains that programs to reduce risk to a community before an emergency are called CRR, or:","community risk reduction",["crowd rescue response","city road repair","career recruit review"],"CRR reduces risk.")
H("752.d.9.A",4,"Community risk reduction aims to:","prevent emergencies and reduce their effects",["end all calls","raise fines","sell insurance"],"CRR prevents harm.")
H("752.d.9.B",3,"A department maps fire frequency, older homes and population to decide where to hold education programs. This is a:","Community Risk Assessment guiding CRR",["parade plan","budget guess","supply count"],"CRA finds risks.")
H("752.d.9.B",4,"A CRA helps a department decide:","which risks and areas need the most attention",["the uniform color","the lunch menu","the parade route"],"CRA directs resources.")
H("752.d.9.C",3,"A fire department partners with schools, a hospital and a housing authority to reduce home fires. These are:","key stakeholders in CRR",["rivals","bystanders","critics only"],"Stakeholders help carry out CRR.")
H("752.d.9.C",4,"The lead agency in a CRR plan is the group that:","coordinates the work and partners",["opposes it","ignores it","funds only"],"The lead agency coordinates.")
H("752.d.9.D",3,"The U.S. Fire Administration's CRR strategies are known as the 5 E's, such as education and enforcement. These are:","five strategies for risk reduction",["five sports","five colors","five classes"],"5 E's: education, engineering, enforcement, economic incentive, emergency response.")
H("752.d.9.D",4,"Installing smoke alarms through a city program is an example of the 5 E's strategy of:","engineering or emergency response support",["entertainment","extravagance","exclusion"],"Engineering uses technology and equipment.")
H("752.d.9.E",3,"City, state and federal agencies use community risk assessments to plan funding and programs. This explains how:","governments use CRAs",["groups ignore data","maps are drawn only","guesses are used"],"CRAs inform policy.")
H("752.d.9.E",4,"A federal agency might use data from many local CRAs to:","target grants and programs",["raise fines","close stations","stop reports"],"Data drives funding.")
H("752.d.10.A",3,"At a big flood response, agencies use the same words, a single plan and clear objectives under NIMS. This describes the:","purpose of NIMS",["school plan","sports plan","menu plan"],"NIMS standardizes response.")
H("752.d.10.A",4,"NIMS stands for:","National Incident Management System",["National Insurance Market Survey","North Island Medical Service","Neighborhood Inspection Map System"],"NIMS coordinates agencies.")
H("752.d.10.B",3,"The Incident Commander, section chiefs and branches make up the:","components of the ICS structure",["school bus route","kitchen crew","cheer squad"],"ICS organizes roles.")
H("752.d.10.B",4,"In ICS, the Incident Commander is responsible for:","overall management of the incident",["only logistics","only finance","only media"],"IC leads the response.")
H("752.d.11.A",3,"A city fire marshal enforces a local fire code and has final say over occupancy. This is the:","authority having jurisdiction (AHJ)",["landlord","tenant","mail carrier"],"AHJ enforces codes.")
H("752.d.11.A",4,"The AHJ is the organization or person that:","has legal authority to enforce codes",["sells equipment","writes the newspaper","owns the building"],"AHJ means jurisdiction.")
H("752.d.11.B",3,"A department chart shows a chief, deputy chiefs, captains, lieutenants and firefighters in order of rank. This is the:","hierarchical structure of a fire department",["lunch line","supply list","parade order"],"Rank structure clarifies authority.")
H("752.d.11.B",4,"In a typical fire department chain of command, a lieutenant reports to a:","captain",["firefighter","recruit","civilian volunteer"],"Lower ranks report up.")
H("752.d.11.C",3,"A fire chief administers the budget, sets policy and represents the department to elected officials. These are the:","roles and responsibilities of the fire chief",["roles of a recruit","roles of a student","roles of a vendor"],"Chiefs lead and manage.")
H("752.d.11.C",4,"The fire chief is primarily accountable for:","the overall operation of the department",["only cleaning","only driving","only training"],"The chief answers for all of it.")
H("752.d.12.A",3,"Inspectors review building plans, check exits and teach fire safety at schools. These are functions of the:","fire prevention division",["training division","vehicle maintenance shop","dispatch center"],"Prevention reduces fires.")
H("752.d.12.A",4,"A fire prevention division conducts:","inspections and public education",["engine repairs","911 calls","academy testing"],"Prevention = inspections and education.")
H("752.d.12.B",3,"A hazmat team and a technical rescue team are part of:","fire service special operations",["clerical staff","grounds crew","cafeteria"],"Special ops handle complex rescues.")
H("752.d.12.B",4,"Special operations units are trained for:","hazardous materials and technical rescues",["parades","fundraisers","classes only"],"They handle unusual hazards.")
H("752.d.12.C",3,"New recruits and veteran firefighters practice skills and take refresher courses through the:","fire training division",["fire prevention division","finance office","dispatch"],"Training keeps skills current.")
H("752.d.12.C",4,"Which task is typically handled by the training division?","coordinating academy classes and drills",["fixing engines","answering 911 calls","inspecting buildings"],"Training runs classes.")
H("752.d.12.D",3,"Mechanics test pumps and repair brakes on engines. These are functions of the:","equipment maintenance division",["training","dispatch","prevention"],"Maintenance keeps rigs ready.")
H("752.d.12.D",4,"The maintenance division makes sure apparatus and tools are:","safe and ready for use",["decorated","hidden","sold"],"Ready equipment saves time.")
H("752.d.12.E",3,"A call taker receives an emergency call, gathers details and sends units. This describes core responsibilities of a:","911 communication center",["print shop","parts room","mess hall"],"911 centers dispatch.")
H("752.d.12.E",4,"A 911 dispatcher's first job on an emergency call is to:","gather the location and nature of the emergency",["end the call","ask for payment","play music"],"Location comes first.")
H("752.d.12.F",3,"During a hurricane, a county office coordinates shelters, resources and agencies. This is the work of the:","Office of Emergency Management",["fire prevention bureau","parks office","library"],"OEM coordinates large disasters.")
H("752.d.12.F",4,"The Office of Emergency Management primarily:","plans for and coordinates disaster response",["fights house fires","writes tickets","repairs engines"],"OEM coordinates across agencies.")
H("752.d.13.A",3,"A science teacher describes a rapid chemical reaction that gives off heat and light and needs fuel, oxygen and heat. This describes:","combustion",["ice","rust","mud"],"Fire = rapid oxidation with heat and light.")
H("752.d.13.A",4,"Fire is best defined as a:","rapid oxidation process that releases heat and light",["slow rusting","frozen reaction","sound wave"],"Combustion is rapid oxidation.")
H("752.d.13.B",3,"The fire triangle has heat, fuel and oxygen, and the fire tetrahedron adds a fourth part. This identifies the:","components of the fire triangle and tetrahedron",["parts of a hose","ladder rails","apparatus"],"The tetrahedron adds the chain reaction.")
H("752.d.13.B",4,"The fourth side of the fire tetrahedron is the:","uninhibited chemical chain reaction",["water","wind","smoke"],"The chain reaction sustains flaming fire.")
H("752.d.13.C",3,"A student sorts ice, water and steam into groups. This describes the physical characteristics of:","the three states of matter",["rock types","fuel types","colors"],"Solid, liquid, gas.")
H("752.d.13.C",4,"Which state of matter has no definite shape or volume?","gas",["solid","liquid","ice"],"Gases fill their container.")
H("752.d.13.D",3,"Oxygen helps a fire burn while wood supplies energy as the burning material. This differentiates an:","oxidizing agent and a fuel",["water and ice","smoke and fog","heat and light"],"Oxidizer + fuel.")
H("752.d.13.D",4,"In a fire, oxygen acts as the:","oxidizing agent",["fuel","heat source","extinguisher"],"Oxygen supports burning.")
H("752.d.13.E",3,"When wood is heated, it gives off flammable vapors before it ignites. This is:","pyrolysis",["evaporation","refrigeration","freezing"],"Pyrolysis is thermal decomposition.")
H("752.d.13.E",4,"Pyrolysis helps fire spread by:","creating flammable gases from solid fuel",["cooling the fuel","removing oxygen","stopping heat"],"Pyrolysis produces vapors.")
H("752.d.13.F",3,"A vapor-air mixture with too much fuel to burn is 'fuel rich', and too little fuel is:","fuel lean",["fuel heavy","fuel cold","fuel wet"],"Flammable range has limits.")
H("752.d.13.F",4,"A fuel-lean mixture contains:","too little fuel to burn",["too much fuel","no air","only water"],"Lean = not enough fuel.")
H("752.d.13.G",3,"A cup of boiling water has a higher temperature than a bathtub of warm water but less total energy. This analyzes the difference between:","temperature and heat",["weight and size","speed and mass","color and shape"],"Temperature is intensity; heat is energy.")
H("752.d.13.G",4,"Heat is best described as:","thermal energy",["a thermometer reading","a measure of speed","humidity"],"Heat is energy transfer.")
H("752.d.13.H",3,"A liquid gives off enough vapor to flash briefly at one temperature and ignites and continues burning at a higher one. This differentiates:","flash point and ignition temperature",["wet and dry","hot and cold","day and night"],"Flash point is lower.")
H("752.d.13.H",4,"The flash point is the lowest temperature at which a liquid:","gives off enough vapor to ignite briefly",["boils","freezes","explodes"],"Flash point = momentary ignition.")
H("752.d.13.I",3,"Gasoline floats on water because its specific gravity is less than 1. This is important because:","burning liquids may spread on water",["water boils off","gasoline sinks","fire is cooled"],"Floating fuel spreads fire.")
H("752.d.13.I",4,"A liquid with a specific gravity greater than 1 will:","sink in water",["float","evaporate","burn"],"Heavier than water sinks.")
H("752.d.13.J",3,"Propane vapors are heavier than air and collect in low areas. This is explained by:","vapor density",["liquid density","air speed","fuel color"],"Vapor density compares gas to air.")
H("752.d.13.J",4,"A vapor density greater than 1 means the vapor will:","sink and collect in low areas",["rise away","float up","disappear"],"Heavier than air.")
H("752.d.13.K",3,"A fire starts small, grows, reaches full burning, then declines. These are the:","stages of fire development",["rules of ethics","parts of a hose","ranks of firefighters"],"Incipient, growth, fully developed, decay.")
H("752.d.13.K",4,"The first stage of fire development is:","incipient",["decay","flashover","fully developed"],"Incipient is the beginning.")
H("752.d.13.L",3,"A sudden ignition of all room contents is a flashover, while a rush of air feeding a starved fire causes a backdraft. This differentiates:","flashover and backdraft",["fuel and heat","smoke and ash","steam and fog"],"Both are rapid fire events.")
H("752.d.13.L",4,"A backdraft is most likely when a firefighter opens a door to a room that is:","oxygen-starved and full of hot gases",["cold and empty","full of water","well ventilated"],"New air can cause backdraft.")
H("752.d.13.M",3,"Heat can move through a metal pipe, by rising hot air, and as waves across a gap. These are the three methods of heat transfer:","conduction, convection and radiation",["rain, snow, wind","day, night, dusk","walking, running, jumping"],"Three ways heat moves.")
H("752.d.13.M",4,"Feeling heat from a bonfire several feet away is an example of:","radiation",["conduction","convection","combustion"],"Radiation travels as waves.")
H("752.d.14.A",3,"A student lists ordinary combustibles, flammable liquids, energized electrical, combustible metals and cooking oils. These are the:","five classes of fire (A, B, C, D, K)",["four seasons","six types of hose","three sides of a triangle"],"Fire classes A, B, C, D, K.")
H("752.d.14.A",4,"A fire involving cooking oils and fats is a:","Class K fire",["Class A fire","Class B fire","Class C fire"],"K = kitchen.")
H("752.d.14.B",3,"Water cools Class A fires while foam smothers Class B fires. These are:","extinguishing methods for the classes of fire",["colors","brands","shapes"],"Each class has proper agents.")
H("752.d.14.B",4,"The best way to extinguish an ordinary wood fire is to:","cool it with water",["smother it with oil","blow on it","cover with sugar"],"Water cools Class A.")
H("752.d.15.A",3,"A city's water system includes a source, treatment plant, pumps, storage tanks and mains. This identifies the:","basic components of a municipal water supply",["parts of a fire truck","parts of a ladder","parts of a boat"],"Municipal water supplies hydrants.")
H("752.d.15.A",4,"Elevated storage tanks in a water system help to:","maintain water pressure",["cool the pipes","clean the streets","launch boats"],"Gravity supports pressure.")
H("752.d.15.B",3,"In cold climates, the valve of a dry barrel hydrant is below ground, while a wet barrel hydrant holds water at all times. This identifies:","types of fire hydrants",["types of hose","types of ladder","types of tool"],"Dry barrel resists freezing.")
H("752.d.15.B",4,"Dry barrel hydrants are common in areas where:","freezing temperatures occur",["it never rains","there is no water","boats are used"],"They drain to prevent freezing.")
H("752.d.15.C",3,"Hydrants with certain colored caps tell firefighters their flow capacity quickly. This explains the:","purpose of hydrant color coding",["paint sale","decoration","fashion"],"Colors show flow.")
H("752.d.15.C",4,"A hydrant's color coding helps firefighters know:","how much water it can supply",["who owns it","what year it was built","its weight"],"Color indicates flow rate.")

# ---- 753 Crisis Intervention and Resilience (first responders) ----
H("753.d.A",3,"A cadet sorts examples of a flat tire, a sudden overwhelming loss and a house fire into groups. This differentiates:","a personal crisis, a problem and an emergency",["a hose, a ladder and a pump","a rank, a badge and a patch","a map, a key and a scale"],"A problem is manageable; a crisis overwhelms coping; an emergency threatens safety now.")
H("753.d.A",4,"Which situation best fits a personal crisis?","a person overwhelmed after a sudden loss who cannot cope",["a flat tire","a missed bus","a spilled drink"],"A crisis overwhelms usual coping skills.")
H("753.d.B",3,"A trainer says a personal crisis usually involves a stressful event, a person's perception of it, and an inability to cope. These are the:","basic elements of a personal crisis",["parts of a hose","steps of a drill","ranks of a station"],"Event + perception + failed coping.")
H("753.d.B",4,"Two people face the same event, but only one has a crisis because of how each:","perceives it and copes",["dresses","eats","commutes"],"Perception shapes crisis.")
H("753.d.C",3,"A counselor lists trauma, family conflict, job loss and illness as things that can trigger a crisis. These are:","factors that may lead to a personal crisis",["rewards","hobbies","fashion trends"],"Many stressors can lead to crisis.")
H("753.d.C",4,"Which is a factor that may contribute to a personal crisis?","the sudden death of a family member",["a new haircut","a sunny day","a new pen"],"Major losses can overwhelm coping.")
H("753.d.D",3,"A student reads how a crisis can affect mental health, emotions, relationships and work. This analyzes the:","impacts of personal crises",["colors of crises","prices of crises","sizes of crises"],"Crises affect many areas.")
H("753.d.D",4,"A prolonged personal crisis can impact a person by:","affecting health, relationships and performance",["improving sleep always","removing all stress","raising grades"],"Wide-ranging impact.")
H("753.d.E",3,"Talk of hopelessness, giving away belongings or threats to hurt oneself are warning signs that need:","immediate attention",["no action","laughing off","waiting a year"],"Serious warning signs need quick help.")
H("753.d.E",4,"If a coworker shows signs of being in immediate danger, the best step is to:","get help right away from trained responders or a crisis line",["wait and see","gossip","post online"],"Immediate danger needs immediate help.")
H("753.d.F",3,"Withdrawal, changes in sleep, drinking more, and missed shifts are signs that someone may need:","intervention and support",["a bonus","a promotion","a day off to travel"],"Indicators suggest a person may need help.")
H("753.d.F",4,"A coworker who suddenly stops joining the crew and misses shifts may need:","a caring check-in and connection to support",["punishment","ridicule","silence"],"Early support helps.")
H("753.d.2.A",3,"A responder offers safety, calm, connection and hope to a person after a disaster, following Psychological First Aid. This applies the:","key principles of Psychological First Aid",["rules of a card game","hose lay steps","ladder rules"],"PFA supports safety, calm, connection, self-efficacy and hope.")
H("753.d.2.A",4,"Psychological First Aid focuses on:","practical support and comfort for people in distress",["diagnosing disorders","deep therapy","punishment"],"PFA is early supportive care.")
H("753.d.2.B",3,"A responder guides an upset person to breathe in slowly, name five things they see, and feel their feet on the floor. These are:","grounding techniques for crisis de-escalation",["parade drills","sports plays","dance moves"],"Grounding returns attention to the present.")
H("753.d.2.B",4,"A slow breathing exercise helps a person in crisis by:","calming the body's stress response",["raising heart rate","increasing panic","distracting from help"],"Slow breathing calms.")
H("753.d.2.C",3,"A responder speaks slowly, uses simple words, repeats the person's name and avoids arguing. These are:","communication techniques for crisis de-escalation",["ways to shout","ways to ignore","ways to hurry"],"Calm, simple talk helps.")
H("753.d.2.C",4,"When de-escalating a person in crisis, a responder should:","speak calmly and listen without judging",["argue","threaten","lecture"],"Listening lowers tension.")
H("753.d.2.D",3,"A responder keeps hands open and visible, an open posture and a respectful distance. This shows how:","body language supports de-escalation",["hiding hands","crossing arms","standing over someone"],"Open body language signals safety.")
H("753.d.2.D",4,"Which body language is more likely to calm a distressed person?","relaxed shoulders, open hands and a respectful distance",["clenched fists","pointing","crowding"],"Nonthreatening posture reassures.")
H("753.d.3.A",3,"A fire chief lists the county mental health authority, a crisis response team and a local counselor's line. These are:","local crisis intervention resources",["food vendors","car dealers","travel agents"],"Local services exist.")
H("753.d.3.A",4,"A mobile crisis outreach team can help a community by:","responding to people in mental health crisis",["selling equipment","painting stations","fixing hoses"],"They send trained clinicians.")
H("753.d.3.B",3,"The Texas Department of State Health Services offers programs and referrals for mental health and substance use help. This identifies:","state crisis resources",["school rules","tax forms","parking permits"],"DSHS provides statewide resources.")
H("753.d.3.B",4,"A statewide agency that can connect Texans to behavioral health services is:","the Texas Department of State Health Services",["the Texas Racing Commission","the Texas Lottery","the Texas Library"],"DSHS supports services.")
H("753.d.3.C",3,"A person in distress can call or text 988 for free, confidential help any time. This is a:","national crisis intervention resource",["pizza hotline","bank number","weather line"],"988 is the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline.")
H("753.d.3.C",4,"The national number to call or text for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline is:","988",["411","311","511"],"988 connects to crisis counselors.")
H("753.d.4.A",3,"A veteran firefighter becomes irritable, has trouble sleeping and avoids the station after a hard call. These could be:","warning signs of a mental health crisis in first responders",["signs of a promotion","signs of fitness","signs of luck"],"Changes in mood and behavior warrant concern.")
H("753.d.4.A",4,"Which change might signal a mental health crisis in a first responder?","withdrawing from friends and crew and losing interest in work",["new hobby only","a day off","a haircut"],"Withdrawal is a warning sign.")
H("753.d.4.B",3,"After a child fatality call, a medic feels flashbacks, guilt and numbness. This analyzes the:","psychological impacts of exposure to trauma",["benefits of hobbies","effects of weather","effects of diet only"],"Trauma exposure has psychological effects.")
H("753.d.4.B",4,"Repeated exposure to trauma can lead first responders to experience:","anxiety, intrusive thoughts and emotional numbness",["only joy","only boredom","no reactions"],"Responders feel impacts too.")
H("753.d.4.C",3,"Headaches, stomach trouble, exhaustion and sleep problems can follow traumatic calls. These are:","physical impacts of trauma exposure",["luck signs","shift rewards","lunch results"],"Stress shows in the body.")
H("753.d.4.C",4,"Chronic trauma-related stress may physically affect a responder by causing:","fatigue and sleep problems",["bigger muscles","better vision","more energy always"],"Stress takes a physical toll.")
H("753.d.4.D",3,"A responder who is distressed after calls snaps at family, avoids friends and feels distant. This explains how trauma-related stress affects:","relationships and social life",["tax rates","vehicle speed","weather"],"Stress strains relationships.")
H("753.d.4.D",4,"One way trauma-related stress can affect a responder's home life is by:","causing withdrawal or conflict with loved ones",["improving all talk","ending all stress","lowering bills"],"Relationships suffer.")
H("753.d.4.E",3,"Trauma-related stress can lead to poor decisions, missed details and slower reactions on the job. This analyzes the effect on:","job performance",["parking","weather","fashion"],"Stress impairs decisions.")
H("753.d.4.E",4,"Which job effect can result from unaddressed trauma stress?","impaired decision-making and attention",["faster promotion","perfect memory","better teamwork"],"Cognition suffers under stress.")
H("753.d.4.F",3,"After a firefighter dies in the line of duty, members may feel grief, guilt and anger. This discusses the psychological impacts of a:","line of duty death (LODD)",["training exercise","budget cut","parade"],"LODD deeply affects the department.")
H("753.d.4.F",4,"After a LODD, a department commonly provides crew members with:","grief support and counseling services",["no response","extra hose","new patches"],"Support helps survivors.")
H("753.d.5.A",3,"After a traumatic call, a trained team holds a group meeting to help responders talk through reactions. This is:","Critical Incident Stress Debriefing and management",["a game","a fire drill","a promotion ceremony"],"CISD/CISM supports responders.")
H("753.d.5.A",4,"The goal of a critical incident stress debriefing is to:","help responders process an event and reduce stress",["assign blame","punish crews","delete memories"],"Debriefings support recovery.")
H("753.d.5.B",3,"A CISM team includes trained peers, a chaplain and a mental health professional. This describes:","roles of CISM team members",["roles of drivers","roles of dispatchers","roles of mechanics"],"CISM teams are multidisciplinary.")
H("753.d.5.B",4,"A peer support member on a CISM team is usually:","a trained fellow first responder",["a stranger with no training","a vendor","a salesperson"],"Peers understand the job.")
H("753.d.5.C",3,"Departments with CISM teams often see better coping, stronger morale and faster recovery. This evaluates the:","benefits of CISM teams in public safety",["costs of ignoring","dangers of help","rules of parking"],"CISM supports responders.")
H("753.d.5.C",4,"A key benefit of a CISM team is that it can:","provide early support and reduce long-term harm",["end all calls","stop all stress","remove duty"],"Early support helps.")
H("753.d.5.D",3,"The National Fallen Firefighters Foundation recognizes interventions like one-on-one support and group sessions. These are:","common CISM interventions",["fire drills","hose tests","awards"],"CISM includes several interventions.")
H("753.d.5.D",4,"A one-on-one peer check-in after a hard call is an example of a:","CISM intervention",["training test","pay rule","parade"],"Individual support is part of CISM.")
H("753.d.5.E",3,"A department invites spouses to an information night on stress, sleep and where to find help. This explains the importance of:","supporting first responder families",["ignoring families","keeping secrets","skipping events"],"Families feel the stress too.")
H("753.d.5.E",4,"Supporting responders' families helps because the family:","shares the stress and can provide support",["has no role","needs no help","is irrelevant"],"Family support is vital.")
H("753.d.6.E",3,"A Local Assistance and Support Team includes mental health professionals, crisis workers and trained peers. This describes the:","composition of a LAST",["structure of a pumper","list of tools","plan of a station"],"A LAST supports survivors after an LODD.")
H("753.d.6.E",4,"Members of a LAST typically include:","mental health professionals and crisis responders",["only chefs","only clerks","only drivers"],"Professional support.")
H("753.d.6.F",3,"After an LODD, a LAST helps the family with funeral logistics, benefits paperwork and counseling. This analyzes the:","functions of a LAST",["functions of a hose","functions of a ladder","functions of a radio"],"A LAST supports survivors.")
H("753.d.6.F",4,"A LAST's primary purpose after an LODD is to:","support survivors and help administer benefits",["investigate fires","repair engines","run drills"],"LAST aids survivors.")
H("753.d.7.A",3,"A candidate for fire department chaplain completes pastoral training, crisis care and department orientation. This describes:","qualifications of a public safety chaplain",["qualifications of a mechanic","qualifications of a pilot","qualifications of a clerk"],"Chaplains need training.")
H("753.d.7.A",4,"A public safety chaplain is typically trained in:","crisis care and ministry to responders",["metalwork","accounting","gardening"],"Chaplains give spiritual support.")
H("753.d.7.B",3,"A department offers peer support, counseling referrals and chaplain visits. These are:","support services for first responders",["fines","chores","penalties"],"Agencies provide support.")
H("753.d.7.B",4,"Which is a support service a first responder organization might provide?","an employee assistance program",["a parking ticket","a fine","a lecture on weather"],"EAPs offer counseling.")
H("753.d.7.C",3,"A chaplain counsels crew members, visits sick family and officiates at memorials. These are the:","roles and responsibilities of public safety chaplains",["tasks of dispatchers","tasks of mechanics","tasks of cooks"],"Chaplains support people.")
H("753.d.7.C",4,"A chaplain may serve a department by:","providing confidential support to members and families",["writing citations","driving engines","teaching hose lays"],"Chaplains offer care.")
H("753.d.7.D",3,"During a mass-casualty event, a chaplain comforts victims' families and stands by crews. This explains the role of chaplains in:","critical incidents and emergencies",["routine parades","budget meetings","paint jobs"],"Chaplains serve during crises.")
H("753.d.7.D",4,"At a major disaster, a chaplain commonly helps by:","providing comfort to victims, families and responders",["fighting the fire","directing traffic","fixing rigs"],"Chaplains give emotional and spiritual care.")
H("753.d.8.A",3,"After a hard season, a firefighter rebounds with support and focus. This explains the concept of:","resilience",["avoidance","fatigue","disregard"],"Resilience is bouncing back.")
H("753.d.8.A",4,"Resilience helps responders cope with stress by:","enabling recovery and adaptation after setbacks",["avoiding all stress","erasing events","ending calls"],"Resilience supports coping.")
H("753.d.8.B",3,"Resilient people often have a positive outlook, strong connections and flexible thinking. These are:","characteristics of resilient individuals",["signs of fatigue","signs of illness","signs of danger"],"Resilient people share traits.")
H("753.d.8.B",4,"One benefit of building resilience is that a person can:","handle stress and recover more effectively",["avoid all challenges","skip work","ignore feelings"],"Resilience helps recovery.")
H("753.d.8.C",3,"A growth mindset and strong self-awareness help a responder stay steady under pressure. These are:","internal factors that contribute to resilience",["external costs","tools","uniforms"],"Mindset and self-awareness build resilience.")
H("753.d.8.C",4,"Self-awareness helps resilience because it lets a person:","notice stress and respond early",["ignore feelings","avoid reflection","skip sleep"],"Awareness enables self-care.")
H("753.d.8.D",3,"A responder builds a support system, uses time management and asks for help when stuck. These are:","strategies to overcome challenges",["ways to give up","ways to quit","ways to hide"],"Strategies support problem-solving.")
H("753.d.8.D",4,"Which is a healthy strategy for overcoming a challenge?","reaching out to a trusted support person",["isolating","ignoring it","blaming others"],"Support helps.")
H("753.d.8.E",3,"A medic who worked through a crisis later says it taught him strength and new coping skills. This shows how a crisis can:","build resiliency and create opportunities for growth",["destroy all growth","end careers","prove weakness"],"Crises can lead to growth.")
H("753.d.8.E",4,"A person who copes well with a past crisis may later:","use what they learned to handle new challenges",["fear all stress","avoid all tasks","lose all skills"],"Experience builds resilience.")
H("753.d.8.F",3,"A responder uses the steps Stop, Think, Observe, Proceed before acting on a tense call. This is the:","STOP method of problem solving",["IDEA method","SMART method","fire triangle"],"STOP slows down and checks the situation.")
H("753.d.8.F",4,"In the STOP method, the 'O' stands for:","observe",["order","obey","operate"],"Observe the situation.")
H("753.d.8.G",3,"A team uses Identify, Develop, Evaluate and Assess to solve a staffing problem. This is the:","IDEA method of problem solving",["STOP method","SMART goal","fire tetrahedron"],"IDEA is a four-step method.")
H("753.d.8.G",4,"In the IDEA method, the 'E' stands for:","evaluate",["exit","enter","erase"],"Evaluate options.")

B.balance()
B.save(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "batches", "cte_98.jsonl"))
